{"name":"Feverish","hex":"#dd6677","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"feverish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a fever, an elevated body temperature.","Filled with excess energy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feverish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fever","blocks":[{"text":"Fever or pyrexia in humans is a symptom of an anti-infection defense mechanism that appears with body temperature exceeding the normal range caused by an increase in the body's temperature set point in the hypothalamus. There is no single agreed-upon upper limit for normal temperature: sources use values ranging between 37.2 and 38.3 °C in humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Symptoms-fever.jpg/330px-Symptoms-fever.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fever","wikidata":"Q38933"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg/500px-Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg/1280px-Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg/500px-Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Febris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVirgil_Solis_Febris.jpg"}],"sounds":{"feverish":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/81/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-feverish.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/81/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-feverish.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-feverish.wav.mp3"},{"t